<% layout('layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<%- include('../partials/nav') %>

<main id="main">
  <section class="page container">
    <h1 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="section-sub">Everything you need to know about voult.dev.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What is voult.dev?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>voult.dev is a developer-first authentication platform. We provide secure APIs, lightweight SDKs, OAuth integrations, magic links, JWT handling, and pre-built UI kits so you can add authentication to your application in minutes instead of weeks.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Why should I use voult.dev over building auth myself?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Building authentication correctly is hard. You need to handle password hashing, JWT rotation, CSRF protection, rate limiting, email verification, password resets, OAuth flows, and session management, all while staying up to date with security best practices. voult.dev handles all of that for you, so you can focus on building your product.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How does voult.dev work?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>voult.dev provides a set of APIs and SDKs that handle the entire authentication lifecycle. You integrate our SDK into your application, configure your auth flows (email/password, OAuth, magic links), and our platform handles the rest. We manage user sessions, token refresh, security events, and provide a dashboard for monitoring.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What frameworks and languages does voult.dev support?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Voult supports Node.js and Express today: <code>@voult/express</code> gives you a mountable auth router, <code>@voult/sdk</code> is the JavaScript client, and <code>@voult/cli</code> scaffolds your configuration. Any frontend (React, Vite, plain HTML) can call the router over fetch. React components and a Next.js integration are planned.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How can I get started with voult.dev?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>The waitlist opens as soon as the launch date is set, and documentation will be published alongside it. The packages are already on npm: <code>@voult/express</code>, <code>@voult/sdk</code> and <code>@voult/cli</code>. For early questions, reach out via our <a href="/contact-us">Contact</a> page.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What's included in the MVP?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>The MVP includes email/password and username sign-in, OAuth (Google, GitHub, Microsoft, Apple, Facebook, LinkedIn), magic links, email verification and password reset, MFA with TOTP and backup codes, passkeys, JWT access tokens with rotating refresh tokens, rate limiting, CSRF protection, an audit log, and a developer dashboard for apps, credentials and OAuth configuration.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How much does voult.dev cost?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Pricing details will be announced closer to launch. For questions about plans or early access, reach out via our <a href="/contact-us">Contact</a> page.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Is voult.dev secure?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Security controls are on by default: bcrypt password hashing, short-lived access tokens with rotating refresh tokens and reuse detection, account lockout after repeated failed logins, rate limiting, CSRF protection, Helmet security headers, IP allowlists, and a risk-scored audit log of authentication events.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Can I self-host voult.dev?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Self-hosting is on our roadmap. Initially, voult.dev will be offered as a managed service for the best developer experience and security guarantees. We're exploring self-hosted options based on community demand.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How can I get help with voult.dev?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>For questions before launch, reach out via our <a href="/contact-us">Contact</a> page or open an issue on our <a href="https://github.com/voult-dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How can I contact voult.dev?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>You can reach us through our <a href="/contact-us">Contact</a> page, or open an issue on our <a href="https://github.com/voult-dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>

    <div class="about-cta-block">
      <h2>Ready to skip the auth grind?</h2>
      <p>Explore the MVP features and see what's coming.</p>
      <a href="/#capabilities" class="btn btn-primary">View features</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
